Statement of changes (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b)):

  * The library is reimplemented in C# and targets .NET Framework 4.7 and
    .NET Standard 2.0, instead of Go.
  * All request/response models and the 639 API method signatures under
    src/DouyinOpenApi/Models and src/DouyinOpenApi/Apis are machine-generated
    from the original Go source file client/client.go by tools/gen_csharp.py.
    Field names, JSON keys and parameter placement (query / body / form /
    multipart) are preserved as-is.
  * Runtime behaviour intentionally differs in several places; see section 12
    of README.md for the full list. Highlights: exponential backoff instead of
    immediate retry, TLS certificate verification enabled by default, GET
    requests sent without a body, and errors exposed with a separate LogId
    field instead of a formatted message string.

